{
  "case_id": "2007-06-1286",
  "document_hash": "b0f6a1f35944289fb353c423e19e34219f7440026d6224c8f4161ac729a395f7",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Peter J. Rubin (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1286",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b0f6a1f35944289fb353c423e19e34219f7440026d6224c8f4161ac729a395f7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b0f6a1f35944-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. RUBIN: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: The question in this case is the meaning of a statute that provides that, in arriving at a trust or estate's adjusted gross income, amounts are allowable in full if they are -- and I quote here from 26 U.S.C. section 67(e), which you can find at the bottom of page 3a of the appendix to the blue brief -- \"costs which are paid or incurred in connection with the administration of the estate or trust and which would not have been incurred if the property were not held in such trust or estate.\" I'd like to make three broad points."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1286",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b0f6a1f35944289fb353c423e19e34219f7440026d6224c8f4161ac729a395f7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b0f6a1f35944-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: I think those three points are certainly what would help me. Could I ask just two preliminary questions? They don't necessarily have to do with this case, just to get something straight. I take it that you couldn't have claimed this deduction under 162 without getting into an argument that it should be capitalized and that's why 212 is in the Code?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1286",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b0f6a1f35944289fb353c423e19e34219f7440026d6224c8f4161ac729a395f7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b0f6a1f35944-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Well, I don't -- I don't really see that line. I mean, let's -- let's take, you know, fixing the roof on a house that's in the trust. Aren't there distinctive trustee obligations with respect to preservation of property, just as there are with respect to preservation of financial assets?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Rubin",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1286",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b0f6a1f35944289fb353c423e19e34219f7440026d6224c8f4161ac729a395f7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b0f6a1f35944-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If it has nothing to do with fiduciary responsibilities, Your Honor, we think it would be a breach of fiduciary obligation to get -- waste the trust money paying for the advice and to act upon it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Rubin",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1286",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b0f6a1f35944289fb353c423e19e34219f7440026d6224c8f4161ac729a395f7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b0f6a1f35944-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We think that this is intended as a categorical rule. And we think that asking that question is in furtherance of these unique obligations and the prudent investor standard, which is not -- this is a new standard that's developed in the United States over the next decade or so."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Rubin",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1286",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b0f6a1f35944289fb353c423e19e34219f7440026d6224c8f4161ac729a395f7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b0f6a1f35944-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I don't think the subjective knowledge of the person from whom one gets the advice is the question."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1286",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b0f6a1f35944289fb353c423e19e34219f7440026d6224c8f4161ac729a395f7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b0f6a1f35944-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There's nothing that I could find anywhere that talked about pass-throughs in respect to the special situation of trusts and estates."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1286",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b0f6a1f35944289fb353c423e19e34219f7440026d6224c8f4161ac729a395f7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b0f6a1f35944-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But have they issued a regulation drawing up this list at this point?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Miller",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1286",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b0f6a1f35944289fb353c423e19e34219f7440026d6224c8f4161ac729a395f7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b0f6a1f35944-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Section 67(e) creates a narrow exception to the 2 percent floor for costs which would not have not have been incurred if the property were not held in trust."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1286",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b0f6a1f35944289fb353c423e19e34219f7440026d6224c8f4161ac729a395f7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b0f6a1f35944-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This is somewhat of a mystery, the wording of that clause."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1286",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b0f6a1f35944289fb353c423e19e34219f7440026d6224c8f4161ac729a395f7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b0f6a1f35944-0001-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Why do you think that the only instances where the expense would not have occurred are those instances where it could not have occurred?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1286",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b0f6a1f35944289fb353c423e19e34219f7440026d6224c8f4161ac729a395f7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b0f6a1f35944-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Now, what about the rest of it? How do you slice up, you know -- now, investment advisor, tell me what percentage of your advice went to the total return and what percentage went to other things."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Mr. Miller)",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1286",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b0f6a1f35944289fb353c423e19e34219f7440026d6224c8f4161ac729a395f7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b0f6a1f35944-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. MILLER: I think the best reading of the proposed regulation, and perhaps the Service may well clarify this during the rule-making process, is that all advice is not unique to trusts because there's no type of advice that a trustee could seek that an individual could not --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1286",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b0f6a1f35944289fb353c423e19e34219f7440026d6224c8f4161ac729a395f7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b0f6a1f35944-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: So how does your customary or commonly incurred test work? Let's say you have two trusts, one $10 million, the other 10,000."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1286",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b0f6a1f35944289fb353c423e19e34219f7440026d6224c8f4161ac729a395f7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b0f6a1f35944-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: May I ask you the same question I asked your adversary? Whether you use the term \"could\" or \"customarily\" or whatever you're formulating, the bottom line, as I understand your position, is that these costs will never be deductible?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1286",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b0f6a1f35944289fb353c423e19e34219f7440026d6224c8f4161ac729a395f7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b0f6a1f35944-0002-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "(Whereupon, at 11:03 a.m., the case in the above-entitled matter was submitted.)"
    },
    {
